# RingCentral Call-Lead Qualification

Owner rules live in the Service concept, not in this rule.

- [ringcentral-call-lead-qualification](../../docs/knowledge/services/ringcentral-call-lead-qualification.md)
- [operations-registry](../../docs/knowledge/services/operations-registry.md)
- [call-lead](../../docs/knowledge/services/call-lead.md)

Software-only notes that are not in those files may stay below (env, ngrok, collection suffix, script names).

- Local setup uses `localhost:3000` exposed through ngrok. `RINGCENTRAL_NGROK_WEBHOOK_URL` may be a bare base URL; `scripts/dev_ops/ringcentral/ringcentral-webhook-create.ts` resolves it to `/api/webhooks/ringcentral`.
- RingCentral collections are resolved by `ringcentral-config.ts`; default mode is test collections with `_test` suffix unless `RINGCENTRAL_COLLECTION_MODE=[REDACTED]`.
- `src/services/ringcentral/call-lead-sources.ts` is migration/test seed data only. Runtime must not import it.
- Inspect with `/api/dev/ringcentral/*` and the `tsx` runners under `scripts/dev_ops/ringcentral/` (no `pnpm ringcentral:*` scripts are wired).
